1
00:00:00,269 --> 00:00:01,288
What happens after you send a

2
00:00:01,288 --> 00:00:02,673
message to a language model?

3
00:00:02,798 --> 00:00:04,077
In this video, we’ll follow a

4
00:00:04,077 --> 00:00:05,558
short prompt through the model, see

5
00:00:05,558 --> 00:00:06,644
how it chooses the next piece

6
00:00:06,644 --> 00:00:08,154
of text, and watch that process

7
00:00:08,154 --> 00:00:08,692
repeat.

8
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,542
A language model receives your prompt

9
00:00:11,542 --> 00:00:13,196
as tokens: pieces of text that

10
00:00:13,196 --> 00:00:14,696
can be words, parts of words,

11
00:00:14,753 --> 00:00:15,792
or punctuation.

12
00:00:15,917 --> 00:00:17,099
Each token becomes a list of

13
00:00:17,099 --> 00:00:17,734
numbers.

14
00:00:17,821 --> 00:00:18,955
Those numbers are the input to

15
00:00:18,955 --> 00:00:19,503
the model.

16
00:00:20,641 --> 00:00:22,891
Inside the model, attention combines information

17
00:00:22,891 --> 00:00:24,083
from earlier tokens.

18
00:00:24,189 --> 00:00:26,064
Other layers transform the result.

19
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:27,535
In the sentence, the cat sat

20
00:00:27,535 --> 00:00:28,814
on the, the model uses the

21
00:00:28,814 --> 00:00:30,487
preceding context to help predict what

22
00:00:30,487 --> 00:00:31,295
might come next.

23
00:00:32,394 --> 00:00:34,067
The output is a probability distribution

24
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:35,567
over possible next tokens.

25
00:00:35,673 --> 00:00:37,356
These numbers are a teaching example.

26
00:00:37,471 --> 00:00:39,144
Mat has forty percent, floor has

27
00:00:39,144 --> 00:00:40,952
thirty, and all other possibilities share

28
00:00:40,952 --> 00:00:41,663
the rest.

29
00:00:41,788 --> 00:00:43,683
A generation rule selects one token.

30
00:00:44,788 --> 00:00:46,500
Suppose the selected token is mat.

31
00:00:46,577 --> 00:00:47,846
It joins the sequence.

32
00:00:47,952 --> 00:00:49,471
The model now predicts another token

33
00:00:49,471 --> 00:00:51,038
using the extended context.

34
00:00:51,144 --> 00:00:52,942
Repeating this process produces a sentence,

35
00:00:53,019 --> 00:00:54,519
a paragraph, or a much longer

36
00:00:54,519 --> 00:00:55,096
reply.

37
00:00:56,186 --> 00:00:57,974
Training adjusts the model parameters using

38
00:00:57,974 --> 00:00:58,782
examples.

39
00:00:58,869 --> 00:01:01,147
During ordinary generation, those learned parameters

40
00:01:01,147 --> 00:01:03,128
stay fixed while the context grows.

41
00:01:03,234 --> 00:01:04,926
A convincing continuation can still be

42
00:01:04,926 --> 00:01:05,532
wrong.

43
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:07,061
Web search and other tools add

44
00:01:07,061 --> 00:01:08,590
separate steps around this process.
